s:
Let the four integers be represented as $x$, $y$, $z$, and $w$, giving us the following modular equations:
\begin{align*}
x &\equiv 3 \pmod{8}, \\
y &\equiv 5 \pmod{8}, \\
z &\equiv 7 \pmod{8}, \\
w &\equiv 1 \pmod{8}.
\end{align*}
To find the remainder when the sum of these integers is divided by $8$, sum the individual remainders:
\begin{align*}
x + y + z + w &\equiv 3 + 5 + 7 + 1 \\
&\equiv 16 \pmod{8}.
\end{align*}
The sum $16$ is exactly divisible by $8$. Therefore, the remainder when the sum of $x$, $y$, $z$, and $w$ is divided by $8$ is $\boxed{0}$.

To solve this, we proceed with polynomial long division:

\[
\begin{array}{c|cc ccc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^2} & +2x & +3 \\
\cline{2-6}
x^2 - 2x + 4 & x^4 & +2x^2 & +1 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{x^4} & -2x^3 & +4x^2 \\
\cline{2-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & +2x^3 & -2x^2 & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & +2x^3 & -4x^2 & +8x \\
\cline{3-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & +2x^2 & -8x & +1 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & +2x^2 & -4x & +8 \\
\cline{4-6}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & -4x & -7 \\
\end{array}
\]

Therefore, the remainder is $\boxed{-4x - 7}$.

